  * Guest memory: the title's work memory (CellVdecResource.memAddr) holds a
  * ring of picture items, 0x200 bytes each: the CellVdecPicItem at +0 and the
  * CellVdecAvcInfo / Mpeg2Info its picInfo points to at +0x80.
+ *
+ * A decoder that does not answer must not freeze a movie (patch 0053). Tekken
+ * 5 DR submits one AU at a time -- the first from the demuxer's AU_FOUND, each
+ * next one from inside AUDONE -- so a decoder thread that never comes back
+ * from Media Foundation leaves the game waiting for ever: the intro movie
+ * stayed white and START did nothing (smoke reach.title, 4 of ~1,400 boots,
+ * all on a PC short of memory and processors). Now:
+ *  - the decoder is made ahead of time (mfh264_prewarm, when the title loads
+ *    the VDEC module ~17 s before the first movie), with 2 decoding threads;
+ *  - every Media Foundation call of the decoder thread is timed; one that
+ *    takes PS3_VDEC_STALL_MS [5000] (0 = never) is abandoned by a watchdog: a
+ *    new decoder thread finishes the AU it was on with a blank picture and
+ *    AUDONE, and the rest of the sequence gets blank pictures -- the movie goes
+ *    on black with its sound, START skips it, its end leads on as usual. The
+ *    old thread, should it ever return, frees its decoder and ends. The next
+ *    sequence tries Media Foundation again (a fresh decoder is made ahead);
+ *  - a decoder that answers but gives no picture for PS3_VDEC_STALL_MS after
+ *    the sequence's first AU (2+ AUs in) is treated the same way;
+ *  - the decoder no longer waits for a full picture queue (8) to drain when the
+ *    title has not taken a picture for 250 ms: it decodes on, up to 16. START
+ *    pressed while the decoder was 8 pictures ahead hung the movie -- the
+ *    title's skip waits for the AUDONE of its last AU before it takes the
+ *    pictures (a decoder made ahead of time is ahead right away).
+ * Test hooks: PS3_VDEC_TEST_STALL=ms (the first AU's decoder call sleeps that
+ * long), PS3_VDEC_TEST_NOPIC=1 (the decoder's pictures are dropped).
  */
 
